#question(title: [A pesky function])[
  Let
  $display(h(x) = cases(x^2 sin frac(thick 1 thick, x) & quad " if " x != 0, 0 & quad " if " x = 0))$.

  + Calculate $display(h' (x))$ for any
    $x != 0$.
  + Using the definition of derivative,
    calculate $display(h' (0))$.
  + Calculate $display(lim_(x -> 0) h' (x))$

     #v(0.2cm)
     #[
       #set text(size: 13pt)
       #emph[Hint:] Questions 2 and 3 have
       different answers.
     ]

  + Is $h$ continuous at $0$?
  + Is $h$ differentiable at $0$?
  + Is $h'$ continuous at $0$?
]
